  "pride_metadata": {
    "project": {
      "accession": "PXD040869",
      "title": "Interspecies interaction reduces selection for antibiotic resistance in Escherichia coli",
      "additionalAttributes": [],
      "projectDescription": "Supernatant from B. subtilis cultures was found to be inhibitory to E. coli MG1655 growth and reduce enrichment of nitrofurantoin-resistant strains in the presence of the antibiotic. Supernatant from six different supernatants with differential effects on E. coli growth was harvested and analysed to identify the protein component responsible for growth inhibition.",
      "sampleProcessingProtocol": "Fully grown cultures of B. subtilis 168 in minimal media with glucose were centrifuged. The supernatant was then concentrated using PierceTM Protein Concentrators with MWCO of 3 KDa. Protein concentration in the concentrated supernatant was determined using Pierce\u2122 BCA Protein Assay Kit (Thermo Scientific) with bovine serum albumin (BSA) solutions as standards. About 40 \u2013 80 \u00b5g of total protein (200\u00b5l) was added to a buffer containing 24 \u00b5l 5% sodium deoxycholate (SDOC) and 12 \u00b5l 1M triethylammonium bicarbonate (TEAB) to get 236 \u00b5l sample. Following reduction with DL-dithiothreitol (DTT), the samples were processed using the modified filter-aided sample preparation (FASP) method (Wisniewski JR et. al. Nat Methods. 2009 May;6(5):359-62). Alkylation of the cysteine residues was performed using 10 mM methyl methanethiosulfonate (MMTS) diluted in digestion buffer (1% sodium deoxycholate (SDC), 50 mM TEAB) for 30 min at room temperature. Samples were double digested with trypsin. Samples were labelled with Tandem Mass Tag (TMT) reagents (Thermo Scientific) according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. The labelled samples were combined, SDC from the pooled sample was removed by acidification with 10% TFA and centrifugation using Pierce\u2122 Peptide Desalting Spin Columns Thermo Fisher Scientific. The sample was eluted with 70\u00b5l+50\u00b5l 50% acetonitrile at 3000xg (5600rpm) for 1-2min. The eluate from the C18 columns containing 130 \u00b5l pure peptides in 70% ACN were dried in a vacuum centrifuge to 5 \u00b5l. Peptide separations were performed using a reversed-phase XBridge BEH C18 column (3.5 \u03bcm, 3.0x150 mm, Waters Corporation) and a linear gradient from 3% to 40% solvent B over 17 min followed by an increase to 100% B over 5 min. Solvent A was 10 mM ammonium formate buffer at pH 10.00 and solvent B was 90% acetonitrile, 10% 10 mM ammonium formate at pH 10.00. The primary fractions were concatenated into the final 10 final fractions (1+11+21+31+41, 2+12+22+32+42, \u2026 10+20+30+40). The final fractions were evaporated and reconstituted in 15 \u03bcl of 3% acetonitrile, 0.2% formic acid for nLC MS analysis.",
      "dataProcessingProtocol": "Identification and relative quantification was performed using Proteome Discoverer version 2.4 (Thermo Fisher Scientific). The reference B. subtilis 168 database was downloaded from Uniprot (September 2021). The database search was performed using the Mascot search engine (Matrix Science, London, UK) with MS peptide tolerance of 5 ppm. Only the unique identified peptides were taken into account for the relative quantification.",
